cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Compartment-Resolved Spatial Transcriptomics of the NSCLC Tumour Immune
  Microenvironment: Primary Lung Tumour vs. Brain Metastasis
message: >-
  If you use this workflow or its derived outputs, please cite it as below, and
  cite the primary data separately (GEO GSE200563; PMID 36216799).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jarrett
    family-names: Evans
    email: jevans2532@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A reproducible Snakemake workflow reanalysing NanoString GeoMx DSP whole
  transcriptome atlas profiles (GEO GSE200563; 120 AOIs, 35 NSCLC patients plus
  7 non-tumour brain controls) to compare the tumour immune microenvironment of
  primary lung tumours with that of matched brain metastases, resolved by
  tissue compartment. A learning and methods project, not intended for
  peer-reviewed publication.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - GeoMx DSP
  - non-small cell lung cancer
  - brain metastasis
  - tumour immune microenvironment
  - Snakemake
  - FAIR
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jjevans25/nsclc-brainmet-time"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-23"
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Primary data source (NanoString GeoMx DSP WTA, GEO GSE200563)
    authors:
      - name: "See PMID 36216799"
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "PMID:36216799"
      - type: other
        value: "GEO:GSE200563"
